#
# Conformance case: teleology/partial-vs-confidence (issue #1055 W1, Task 5).
#
# An optimization goal recorded as PartiallySatisfied carrying a logic:satisfactionDegree, held strictly APART from a separate Satisfied evaluation carrying a low logic:confidence: the partial/degree axis and the confidence axis stay distinct (a degree is never folded into a truth value, a confidence is never read as a degree).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/partial-vs-confidence/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
